From 9b19174cfec7a893c37971720ae0c9d31aed73e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 19:42:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: free-text-first answer flow for exercises and contest
 questions
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

New spec: exercises/contest questions shouldn't jump straight to multiple
choice. The student first types their own answer; only after failing gets
the existing hint + multiple-choice flow. This adds the piece needed to
make that possible without touching the existing hint/XP system at all.

- Added an optional Exercise.reponseTexte / ContestQuestion.reponseTexte
  field (nullable — content without it skips straight to the existing QCM
  flow, so this is fully backward compatible with everything already
  built).
- GET /exercises/:id and GET /contests/:id now expose only a
  hasReponseTexte boolean, never the actual text — the correct answer
  string is never sent to the client until it's been earned.
- New POST /exercises/:id/check-answer and
  POST /contests/sessions/:sessionId/questions/:questionId/check-answer:
  case/whitespace-insensitive exact match against the stored text,
  server-side only.
  - Correct: records the attempt, awards full XP (no hints have been shown
    yet at this point, so no penalty), returns the solution — mirrors
    submitAnswer's bookkeeping exactly.
  - Wrong (exercises): recorded as a failed ExerciseAttempt for the same
    analytics reasons wrong QCM submissions already are.
  - Wrong (contests): deliberately NOT recorded. ContestSessionAnswer has
    a unique [sessionId, questionId] constraint — writing a row for a
    wrong guess would permanently block the real submission for that
    question. Only a correct guess ever writes a row.
- Admin exercise/contest-question forms get a new optional "Réponse
  attendue (texte libre)" field, flowing through the existing DTOs with
  no other backend plumbing needed (both create/update paths already
  spread the DTO into the Prisma write).

175/175 tests passing (20/20 suites): findOne leak checks (never exposes
the raw text), correct/incorrect matching with normalization, the
no-row-on-wrong-guess contest behavior specifically, and unconfigured
(null) exercises/questions correctly rejecting the check-answer call.
